---
import Reading from "../components/Reading.astro";
import { profile } from "../data/profile";

const langs = profile.languages.map((l) => l.language).join(", ");
---

<Reading
  title="About"
  description={`About ${profile.name} — ${profile.title}`}
>
  <p class="eyebrow">About me</p>
  <h1>{profile.name}</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    I build software for people who can't afford for it to go down — clinics with
    unreliable power, field workers with no signal, government systems that can't have
    gaps in the record. My background is unusual for a web developer: five-plus years
    keeping government infrastructure running, before I ever shipped a line of code for a
    client. That's exactly where the obsession with reliability comes from.
  </p>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <h2>Who I am</h2>
  <p>
    I'm Abdullah Tayyab — online as <strong>Ellife Dash</strong> — a full-stack
    developer based in {profile.location}, working remotely with clients anywhere. For
    five-plus years I've operated critical infrastructure for Punjab Police by day, and
    spent my off-hours building real software for real problems: clinic systems,
    citizen-facing healthcare tools, monitoring tools, and whatever else a local problem
    actually needed.
  </p>
  <p>
    I care less about flashy interfaces and more about software that works offline,
    loads fast, and respects the person using it. This site reflects that: quiet,
    readable, substance over spectacle.
  </p>

  <h2>What I do</h2>
  <p>
    I build full-stack web applications with the MERN stack, offline-first PWAs, desktop
    apps with Electron, and Chrome extensions — whatever the problem calls for. I still
    run and maintain internal government platforms on the side, which is where the
    obsession with reliability actually comes from.
  </p>

  <h2>How I think</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Offline-first.</strong> Networks fail; software shouldn't fail with them.</li>
    <li><strong>Readable over clever.</strong> Code and copy should make sense to someone else in six months — including future me.</li>
    <li><strong>Small, sharp tools.</strong> Solve the real problem, then stop building.</li>
  </ul>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <div class="callout">
    <h3 style="margin-bottom:8px">Currently</h3>
    <p class="muted">
      Finishing my BSc in Computer Science at Virtual University of Pakistan, and working
      through CS50 and freeCodeCamp on the side. Always up for a conversation about
      offline-first architecture, clinic software, or government tech.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:16px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/connect">Work with me</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/experience">See my experience</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="aside">
    <div class="aside-block">
      <span class="label">Quick facts</span>
      <ul class="aside-list">
        <li><strong>Role:</strong> {profile.title}</li>
        <li><strong>Based in:</strong> {profile.location} (remote-friendly)</li>
        <li><strong>Experience:</strong> 5+ yrs in systems operations, 2+ yrs building software</li>
        <li><strong>Languages:</strong> {langs}</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="aside-block">
      <span class="label">Get my CV</span>
      <ul class="aside-list">
        <li><a href="/assets/Abdullah-Tayyab-Resume_2026.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Download PDF ↗</a></li>
        <li><a href="/assets/resume_.docx" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Download DOCX ↗</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="aside-block">
      <span class="label">Online</span>
      <ul class="aside-list">
        <li><a href={profile.links.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a></li>
        <li><a href={profile.links.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn ↗</a></li>
        <li><a href={profile.links.instagram} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Instagram ↗</a></li>
        <li><a href={profile.links.behance} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Behance ↗</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</Reading>
